{"cwd": "/tmp/flyrig-sandboxes/20260815T052807/websearch-tool", "duration_ms": 6682, "hook_event_name": "PostToolUse", "permission_mode": "bypassPermissions", "prompt_id": "b5356d1f-c0c0-4480-b7cd-4849174d7294", "session_id": "<SESSION_ID>", "tool_input": {"query": "claude code hooks"}, "tool_name": "WebSearch", "tool_response": {"durationSeconds": 6.681674693000001, "query": "claude code hooks", "results": [{"content": [{"title": "GitHub - disler/claude-code-hooks-mastery: Master Claude Code Hooks · GitHub", "url": "https://github.com/disler/claude-code-hooks-mastery"}, {"title": "Claude Code Hooks. Deterministic Control Over… | by Cobus Greyling | Medium", "url": "https://cobusgreyling.medium.com/claude-code-hooks-f5a4a8b0e53c"}, {"title": "Claude Code hooks explained: the missing layer between prompts and production", "url": "https://joseparreogarcia.substack.com/p/claude-code-hooks-explained-the-missing"}, {"title": "Claude Code Hooks: The Developer’s Secret Weapon for AI-Controlled Automation | by Narmadha | Towards AI", "url": "https://pub.towardsai.net/claude-code-hooks-the-developers-secret-weapon-for-ai-controlled-automation-0a0aaeb7ef7d?gi=20bc692cbdb2"}, {"title": "Hooks reference - Claude Code Docs", "url": "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks"}, {"title": "Claude Code Hooks Complete Guide - Deterministic Enforcement Across the Tool Lifecycle | hidekazu-konishi.com", "url": "https://hidekazu-konishi.com/entry/claude_code_hooks_complete_guide.html"}, {"title": "Claude Code hooks 是用户定义的 shell 命令,在 Claude Code 生命周期的各个点执行。Hooks 提供对 Claude Code 行为的确定性控制,确保某些操作总是发生,而不是依赖 LLM 选择运行它们。", "url": "https://docs.anthropic.com/zh-CN/docs/claude-code/hooks-guide"}], "tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_0142SECSHZcVpM2TLRjj7zmc"}, "Based on the search results, here's what Claude Code hooks are:\n\n## Overview\n\nHooks are user-defined shell commands, HTTP endpoints, or LLM prompts that execute automatically at specific points in Claude Code's lifecycle. Hooks are shell commands that Claude Code executes at specific lifecycle events. They run outside the model. They are not interpreted by the AI.\n\n## Why Hooks Matter\n\nA system prompt is a request. A hook is a guarantee. Hooks make the enforcement deterministic where the prompt makes it probabilistic. This is important because under complex multi-step reasoning, edge cases, or adversarial inputs, prompt-based guardrails can fail.\n\n## How They Work\n\nA hook starts with an event, can optionally be narrowed with a matcher, receives structured input from Claude Code, and then executes one or more handlers. The AI doesn't know hooks exist. It can't override them. This is what makes hooks so powerful.\n\n## Common Use Cases\n\nSecurity enhancements block dangerous commands and sensitive file access at multiple levels, automatic logging logs all hook events as JSON, and personalized experiences use engineer names from environment variables."], "searchCount": 1}, "tool_use_id": "toolu_01JZqGcPTBwhU5YnyYRC2PBq", "transcript_path": "<TRANSCRIPT_PATH>"}
